      "writtenOn": "2021-11-08T05:52:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks dangerous to do in a general utility.\n\n- If the main handler thread of the test is not started, I think this crashes (or at least, it won\u0027t run the callback test)\n- If you call expectSystemDefaultNetwork from the handler thread, future.get() will block it and prevent the callback from running\n\nYou can\u0027t know what situation the caller is in, so I don\u0027t think it\u0027s okay to do this.\n\nYou could have the caller pass a handler instead.",
